    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a constrained utility profile as we navigate a heavy schedule of off-days. With elite speed threats like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** unavailable due to the team\u2019s light calendar, we are forced to lean on **Christian Yelich** in the UTIL spot today. His projected score of 49.84 reflects a marginal start, heavily tempered by a difficult matchup against Pivetta, whose 3.17 xERA suppresses the offensive ceiling. While **Christian Yelich** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed starter\u2014adding 13% to his base efficiency\u2014the park factors and the pitcher\u2019s command keep him firmly in the \"marginal\" territory rather than a must-start asset.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the coaching staff today involved **Gary Sanchez**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a score of 38.05. Despite a favorable lineup position (#5) providing a slight 2% boost, **Gary Sanchez** could not overcome the negative drag of facing Pivetta\u2019s elite skill set, which cratered his projection by 19%. The optimizer ultimately favored the higher positional flexibility and platoon upside offered by **Christian Yelich**. We remain in a holding pattern with the rest of our core, including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Carson Benge**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom are sidelined today. With no major weather concerns in the forecast, the primary risk remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Christian Yelich**, which introduces a slight uncertainty in his actual batting order position and, consequently, his total plate appearance projection.",
